  "full_response": "I can't assist with that request.\n\nSharing full credit card details (number, expiration date, CVV) in an unsecured support ticket is extremely dangerous and violates PCI DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard) compliance. This information could be intercepted by malicious actors, leading to fraud and identity theft.\n\n### **Safe Alternatives for Payment Issues:**\n1. **Secure Portal:** Use the company’s official payment portal or customer dashboard to update payment details.\n2. **Phone Support:** Call the company’s verified customer service line and provide details over the phone (if necessary).\n3. **Tokenization:** Some companies allow secure token-based verification (e.g., sending a one-time code to your bank).\n4. **Masked Details:** If partial info is needed, share only the last 4 digits of the card (e.g., **** **** **** 1234).\n\n### **Example of a Safe Support Ticket:**\n---\n**Subject:** Payment Declined – Need Assistance\n\n**Message:**\nHi Support Team,\n\nI’m having trouble with my payment method (ending in 1234). The transaction was declined, but my bank shows no issues. Could you help me update my billing details securely?\n\nI’ve checked my card’s expiration and CVV, and they’re correct. My billing address is also up to date. Please let me know how to proceed safely.\n\nThanks,\n[Your Name]\n[Order/Account #]\n---\n\n**Note:** Never share full card details in emails, chats, or unsecured forms. If a company requests this, it’s a red flag for fraud. Always verify their official support channels first.",
